# No `sm:` Tailwind Breakpoints

Opensource UI uses a **two-step** responsive system. Do **not** use `sm:` anywhere in this project — components, marketing, or docs.

## Use instead

1. **Base (default)** — mobile / small screens
2. **`md:`** — tablet and larger (covers `lg:` and up)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="px-3 sm:px-4 md:px-6" />
<div className="w-64 sm:w-80 md:w-96" />
<div className="hidden sm:block" />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="px-3 md:px-6" />
<div className="w-64 md:w-96" />
<div className="hidden md:block" />
```

## Why

`sm:` breakpoints are unreliable in this project's Tailwind v4 setup. Base styles target mobile; `md:` handles all larger viewports. This is part of the Opensource UI design system (`skills/opensource-ui/references/design.md`).
